From 96ef183e05f35d1a84c2817030c5a158f21a7dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:31:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Make the monitor itself the 3D area, in place of the
 separate 3D window

The 3D entry of the monitor menu's Stereoscopic 3D > Preview (offered under a compositor that
takes stereo content declarations) turns the monitor's video area into a 3D area of Kdenlive's own
window. StereoLayer, in place of the window of the first version, is a wl_subsurface of the main
window's surface placed below it, at the rectangle of the monitor widget, holding both views side
by side with the left eye first (each at the size of the area, black where its shape is not the area's)
and declared as full side by side. The views come from the stereo3d_unpack filter on the monitor's
consumer, which takes them out of the full colour picture of every packing, a frame sequence paired
from consecutive frames, and which is only there while the 3D area is.

The main window then has an alpha buffer (Qt::WA_TranslucentBackground), paints its own background
except under a 3D area, and the monitor, transparent over its area (the clear colour, and no video drawn),
keeps drawing its ruler and overlays: they are on the screen plane, the same in both eyes, as is everything
else in the window. The monitor keeps the layer's rectangle when it moves or is resized.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
